The private `/api/game/evidence/upload` endpoint authenticates every begin/page/commit command and checks the current runtime fence inside the evidence transaction. Begin immediately blocks retrieval of the previous document and cancels legacy queued external work. New selection-aware attempts cannot dispatch or complete through that barrier, as described below. Page retries are immutable and idempotent; incomplete, conflicting, cross-scope, stale-runtime or corrupt documents cannot replace active evidence. Commit checks all pages, canonical UTF-8 hashes, counts, source revisions and consent high-water marks before atomic promotion. Expired staging discards duplicate text but preserves the privacy barrier. Capacity deferral also persists that barrier. An existing game database is backed up before the staging schema is added; no live store was migrated during implementation.

The shared client automatically pages large projections, signs each bounded request, resumes acknowledged pages on a later worker attempt, validates every acknowledgment and the final receipt, and checks current authorization and source content between requests. Unicode canonicalization matches Python, including supplementary-plane characters. A cross-language fixture transferred and promoted 2,050 sources and replayed the completed receipt without another commit.

